  "slug": "artist:mayhem",
  "name": "Mayhem",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in Oslo in 1984 by guitarist Øystein 'Euronymous' Aarseth and bassist Jørn 'Necrobutcher' Stubberud, Mayhem became a foundational act in the early Norwegian black metal scene. The band's history is marked by extreme turbulence, including the 1991 suicide of vocalist Per Yngve 'Dead' Ohlin and the 1993 murder of Euronymous by Varg Vikernes. Despite these events, the group continued, releasing influential works such as the 1994 debut De Mysteriis Dom Sathanas and the 2007 Spellemann Award-winning album Ordo Ad Chao. Their sound has evolved from raw, punk-influenced black metal—evident on the 1987 Deathcrush EP—to more experimental and progressive compositions featured on later records like 2019's Daemon. The ensemble currently maintains a lineup featuring long-time drummer Jan Axel 'Hellhammer' Blomberg alongside vocalists and guitarists like Attila Csihar and Teloch.",
